# Generated output is tracked: the kit is audited by readers who do not run it.

# Generated at run time, never committed: RUN_ME_FIRST.praat carries a macOS
# include path because that is where the plugin installs for its audience.
# Praat's `include` is a parse-time text paste, so the path cannot be a
# variable and a Linux run needs its own copy of the file. Committing that
# copy would create a second runner free to drift from the first, and the
# two would disagree silently. Regenerate it instead:
#
#   sed 's|~/Library/Preferences/Praat Prefs/|~/.praat-dir/|' \
#       RUN_ME_FIRST.praat > RUN_KIT_LINUX.praat
#
RUN_KIT_LINUX.praat
probe_results.txt
